---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Growvidence"
  description="Privacy information for Growvidence: browser-local learning data, no accounts, analytics, uploads or app-set cookies."
>
  <article class="privacy-content">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Last updated: 25 November 2026</strong>
    </p>

    <h2>Learning data stays in this browser</h2>
    <p>
      Tracks, tasks, journal entries, and your theme preference are stored in
      this browser's IndexedDB. The app's code is designed to keep learner
      records on this device; it does not send them to a Growvidence backend.
      Browser storage is not a backup and can be cleared or lost.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No user accounts or sign-in.</li>
      <li>No analytics.</li>
      <li>The app does not set cookies.</li>
      <li>No learner-record uploads.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Third-party requests</h2>
    <p>
      In the source files reviewed for this privacy update, we did not identify
      third-party runtime requests from the app. This is a limited source
      review: the generated site and live browser network traffic were not
      independently inspected as part of this change.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site includes a Google Search Console verification meta tag. That
      static verification tag itself does not collect visitor data or make a
      tracking request.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The public website is hosted by GitHub Pages. GitHub may process technical
      hosting logs, such as information about requests, as part of operating its
      services. Read{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement">
        GitHub's Privacy Statement
      </a>{" "}
      for information about GitHub's processing and privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      In the learner workspace, use Delete on a track, task or journal entry to
      move it to deleted records, then use Permanently delete for that record.
      Permanent deletion cannot be undone.
    </p>
    <p>
      To remove the app's stored data from your browser, clear the site data for{" "}
      <code>manayab.github.io</code> in your browser settings. This removes the
      local Growvidence database, including records you have not permanently
      deleted in the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      Backup/export, import/restore and a dedicated delete-all-data feature are
      planned but are not implemented.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions: open an issue at{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/MANayab/Growvidence/issues">
        https://github.com/MANayab/Growvidence/issues
      </a>{" "}
      or email <a href="mailto:manayab2@gmail.com">manayab2@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-content {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: #a43618;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .eyebrow {
      color: #ff987c;
    }
  }
</style>
